    {
      "extraction_class": "NORM",
      "extraction_text": "Las escaleras que comuniquen sectores de incendio diferentes pero cuya altura de evacuación no exceda de la admitida para las escaleras no protegidas, no precisan cumplir las condiciones de las escaleras protegidas, sino únicamente estar compartimentadas de tal forma que a través de ellas se mantenga la compartimentación exigible entre sectores de incendio, siendo admisible la opción de incorporar el ámbito de la propia escalera a uno de los sectores a los que sirve.",
      "attributes": {
        "id": "c1d5e6f7-8a9b-0c1d-2e3f-4a5b6c7d8e9f",
        "parent_section_id": "ee397064d26313e4",
        "paragraph_number": 2,
        "obligation_type": "MANDATORY",
        "norm_statement": "Staircases connecting different fire sectors, but whose evacuation height does not exceed that permitted for unprotected staircases, do not need to comply with the conditions for protected staircases. They only need to be compartmentalized to maintain the required compartmentalization between fire sectors, with the option of incorporating the staircase area into one of the sectors it serves.",
        "applies_if": "STAIRCASE.CONNECTS_DIFFERENT_FIRE_SECTORS == TRUE AND STAIRCASE.EVACUATION.HEIGHT <= UNPROTECTED_STAIRCASE.MAX_EVACUATION_HEIGHT",
        "satisfied_if": "STAIRCASE.IS_COMPARTMENTALIZED_TO_MAINTAIN_FIRE_SECTOR_COMPARTMENTALIZATION == TRUE ; OR STAIRCASE.AREA.INCORPORATED_INTO_SERVED_FIRE_SECTOR == TRUE",
        "exempt_if": "FALSE",
        "topics": [
          "SAFETY.FIRE",
          "SAFETY.USE"
        ],
